{
  "id": "T-MODSGATE",
  "title": "MODS-GATE-1 (user-approved 2026-09-29): the host's lobby 'Different mods' Allow/Refuse. (1) Allow = today: a mismatched joiner (DEV 'fakemod' on both sides: host-only ModsGateHostOnly, client-only ModsGateClientOnly) joins with the MOD MISMATCH warning; (2) Refuse through the button's click path is saved; the same joiner is refused at Hello and its log / Couldn't join card carries the approved sentence; (4) matching mods + Refuse joins normally; (3) mid-game (host loaded ${session}) with Refuse the mismatched join is refused and never parked (acceptjoin: none pending); (5) a host restart keeps Refuse. MODS-FOLD (review 2026-09-29): (a) Refuse never refuses on a folder-derived list and an empty completed scan is '(none)' whatever folders are on disk; (b) re-check fold: while the host's mod list is NOT ready (DEV 'fakemod busy', through the one readiness function) a mismatched joiner under Refuse is admitted as Allow with the 'not ready' line - never held, never refused; once ready the same joiner is refused. Decision 22: each refusal tells the host 'X was turned away: different mods.' (lobby notice / in-game toast, at most one per player per 30 s). Restores Allow and clears the fake mods.",
  "preconditions": "Dev build with the 'uiview modsgate' and 'fakemod' levers (TestDrive.cs / MPCanvasUI.DevUi). Fixture save1 (host melaus, client Client1). Both instances share one ModsLocal, so the real mod lists match; the difference comes only from 'fakemod'.",
  "instances": 2,
  "vars": {
    "clientPid": "Client1",
    "hostPid": "melaus",
    "session": "save1"
  },
  "oracles_absent": [
    "\\[Server\\] mid-game join request from 'Client1'",
    "\\[Server\\] returning player 'Client1' auto-accepted",
    "\\[Server\\] mods refusal for ",
    "\\[MenuUI\\] Different mods: ",
    "\\[MenuUI\\] lobby refresh: ",
    "\\[MenuUI\\] lobby tick: ",
    "\\[MenuUI\\] BuildLobbyWindow: ",
    "\\[TestDrive\\] uiview: ",
    "\\[TestDrive\\] screenshot: ",
    "\\[Config\\] RefuseModMismatch save: ",
    "\\[Server\\] Hello from .*mods verdict held",
    "\\[Mods\\] mods-panel apply tracking NOT bound",
    "\\[Mods\\] mods-panel apply tracking check failed"
  ],
  "oracles_report": [
    "\\[Config\\] Different mods",
    "\\[MenuUI\\] Different mods",
    "\\[Server\\] Hello from ",
    "\\[Content\\] MOD MISMATCH",
    "\\[Client\\] disconnect reason tag",
